JavaScript `using` and `await using` declarations are listed like `const`.
The TypeScript grammar this build uses predates `using`, so this holds for JavaScript files only.
== args
input/resources.js
== file input/resources.js
using handle = open("a");
await using connection = connect();
== stdout
input/resources.js
[L1-L1] using handle
[L2-L2] await using connection
== stderr
== exit 0
